description.narrative:
The activity will support the programme  on Strengthening, Access to Information, Accountability of Institutions and media Competence in Uzbekistan, including support in development of a national MIL strategy for Uzbekistan. The activity aims to assess the level of competence and awareness of MIL and build capacities of policy and decision-makers on MIL to prepare the ground to develop a comprehensive MIL strategy with the Government of Uzbekistan. To do so, the activity is aimed at: 

1) Conducting research assessment to produce MIL Background Document to evaluate the current state of media and information literacy in Uzbekistan among the government and public (1 document); 
2) Conducting a series of national consultations to ensure a comprehensive and inclusive approach to improving MIL in Uzbekistan (10 consultations);
3) Implementing targeted workshops and trainings of trainers for governmental stakeholders, judicial actors and law enforcement bodies, journalists and bloggers with a strong regional component. The training material will be carefully tailored to the Uzbek context and implemented in collaboration with local and regional partners (2 trainings/workshops);
4) Organizing high-level dialogues at the national and regional levels to promote collaboration and coordination among stakeholders, exchange ideas and perspectives, and identify potential solutions and strategies to promote MIL in Uzbekistan in the form of National Position Paper serving as a roadmap leading to the development of the MIL strategy (5 dialogues)
5) Facilitating the development of a National MIL Strategy in Uzbekistan through the involvement of all relevant stakeholders (1 MIL Strategy).
